Sol / Lares (Tasked Spirit).

* ''CLOSED — MEASURED, ralias HIGH.'' The catalog bridge still admits the alias, but the composed private-document verdict denies face A access to face B’s circles. Actual `faceOf` wiring preserves each face’s own access. Foreign ownership refuses before consulting permissive gates.
* ''CLOSED — MEASURED, rcx HIGH.'' A fully signed `[self, A, B]` reveal using ''self + A'' now fails full-chain verification and is set aside by the fold. Uppercase keys and subsequent graft reveals also refuse. Valid outside-contact quorums and pre-enrolment self recovery pass.
* ''CLOSED at the probed boundary — MEASURED, porch5 × ralias.'' All ten face-plane IDs, daemon ID and catalog ID refuse before binding or spec registration. The composed fence → typed denial → delegation → resolver path returns `wiki-mount-refused: no-read-grant`, teaches no private spec, clears its pending delegation and aborts its signal. An ordinary wiki passes.

''No new HIGH or adverse cross-lane interaction found'' in the revisions against the landed porch5 span.

Verification used source overlays in memory: 21 recovery cases and eight guard/resolver cases passed, plus the direct composition probes above. These were assertion-harness probes, not a Vitest receipt. Three disk-writing cases were skipped. ''Lead runs:'' full worker materialization and confirmation that no foreign tiddlers appear.

Writing `out.md` was rejected by the read-only sandbox; escalation is prohibited. The handback is therefore here.

